From d68925f9cd5fbda3fed2c3fcb1ded2a703964826 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: justr4mzi <ramzihouhou8@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:24:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 27/29] texture_cache, astc_decoder: cheaper ASTC uploads (from
 SmileyTatsu's fork) (#296)

* texture_cache: scan new ASTC data where it is instead of copying it first

The opacity scan copied the whole guest range into astc_scan_buffer and the
upload then read it again. GpuGuestMemory hands out the guest memory directly
when the range is in one piece and falls back to the scratch buffer when it is
split, so the scan no longer copies in the common case.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 (implementation)
(cherry picked from commit 87da314115bd91b7950b8597f68af0098b8fefc9)

* astc_decoder: compute the weight scale and partition hash once per block

The per-texel weight scale and the partition hash setup only depend on the
block, so they are computed once per block instead of once per texel, and the
colour range search (which had a TODO to try bisection) is a bisection now: the
bit length never decreases with the encoding index. The output is bit-identical
to the previous decoder on millions of random blocks of every footprint, which
was compared on a GPU.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 (implementation and bit-exact comparison harness)
(cherry picked from commit ab2fd96ded3196f7b7c593b083349904559d1733)

---------

Co-authored-by: SmileyTatsu <185381457+SmileyTatsu@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit d590d51820f99447bd7056920e28eaeab510e4f1)
(cherry picked from commit 13066e0042b21934f6915a4c4d2cbcbe79d9c4be)
